{
  "id": 473090967,
  "iid": 24342,
  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Cleanups to the interface listing code.",
  "description": "Make some routines static that aren't used outside\ncapture/capture-pcap-util.c.\n\nget_interface_list_ss() doesn't return any interfaces, as it passes\nfalse to as the first argument to get_interface_list_findalldevs(), and\nif thar argument is false, it doesn't call anything tha returns any\ninterfaces, it just returns an empty list of interfaces. Make\nget_interface_list_ss() do that directly, with common code both on\nWindows and non-Windows systems.\n\nGiven that, the first argument to get_interface_list_findalldevs() is\nalways true, so get rid of it.\n\nWhile we're at it, fix a comment to note that a vendor description for\nan interface is provided only on Windows.\n\nAI-Assisted: no",
  "state": "merged",
